.git
# **-prefixed so the workspace's web/app/node_modules is excluded too
# (audit 16 #434). A bare `node_modules` is anchored to the context root,
# so a dev machine's web/app tree -- pnpm symlinks into a store that IS
# excluded, plus Vite's .vite cache -- was uploaded into the context and
# copied over the builder's fresh install, breaking `build: .` builds.
**/node_modules
.vscode
.env
.DS_Store
*.sketch
config.yaml
# Repo metadata + docs are not part of the runtime image (audit 12 #267).
# Excluding them trims the build context so `docker build` uploads less
# from the local checkout to the daemon.
tests/
# Test-config files at the repo root (audit 13 #348). tests/ excludes
# the test sources themselves, but the configs that wire vitest +
# tsconfig.test.json into the build context are separate files; without
# excluding them, every Docker build pushes them through the context
# even though `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --prod` never reads them.
tsconfig.test.json
vitest.config.ts
.github/
docs/
*.markdown
CHANGELOG.md
RELEASE_NOTES.markdown
# `dist/` is excluded from the build context, but the multi-stage
# Dockerfile produces its own `dist/` INSIDE the builder image and the
# runtime image copies it via `COPY --from=builder /app/dist ./dist`.
# `COPY --from=<stage>` bypasses .dockerignore by design, so the runtime
# image always ships a freshly-built bundle -- excluding a stale local
# `dist/` here just prevents it from polluting the context (audit 9 #124).
dist/
data/
secrets/
web/app/dist
